WEBVTT

00:00:14.430 --> 00:00:19.060
For the happiness of all, to create a world full of bliss,

00:00:19.760 --> 00:00:21.980
I will make use of your life.

00:00:22.230 --> 00:00:24.020
Garrod, what are you doing?!

00:00:24.690 --> 00:00:26.600
Get up! Get on your feet!

00:00:26.690 --> 00:00:27.770
Get out of there, Garrod!

00:00:27.810 --> 00:00:29.020
You'll be killed!

00:00:29.770 --> 00:00:31.070
Garrod!

00:00:31.360 --> 00:00:34.320
Come on, get on with it! Finish him off!

00:00:40.410 --> 00:00:43.500
You said something fascinating earlier.

00:00:44.370 --> 00:00:47.250
That my being a Newtype is all the more reason for you not to lose.

00:00:47.830 --> 00:00:51.210
I'm sorry, but reality is cruel.

00:00:51.840 --> 00:00:54.380
Old humanity cannot defeat me!

00:00:55.380 --> 00:00:56.720
Garrod!

00:01:01.560 --> 00:01:06.850
<b>After War</b>

00:01:01.560 --> 00:01:06.850
<b>GUNDAM</b>

00:01:06.850 --> 00:01:14.360
<b>The dream I'd nearly forgotten is beginning to stir,</b>

00:01:14.360 --> 00:01:17.320
<b>little by little</b>

00:01:17.320 --> 00:01:21.870
<b>filling in the gaps in my heart</b>

00:01:21.870 --> 00:01:29.250
<b>The instant my frozen memories begin to awaken,</b>

00:01:29.250 --> 00:01:38.760
<b>my only wish is for the future that is about to begin</b>

00:01:38.760 --> 00:01:42.310
<b>I'll reach out with both hands</b>

00:01:42.310 --> 00:01:46.310
<b>and embrace that dream I once had</b>

00:01:46.310 --> 00:01:49.940
<b>I want to go on believing</b>

00:01:49.940 --> 00:01:53.860
<b>without ever letting go or giving up</b>

00:01:53.860 --> 00:01:57.490
<b>Until the day comes when I grab hold...</b>

00:01:57.490 --> 00:02:01.370
<b>...of that dream I once had,</b>

00:02:01.370 --> 00:02:04.910
<b>I want to keep chasing after it</b>

00:02:04.910 --> 00:02:10.790
<b>without ever forgetting my hopes and dreams</b>

00:02:15.420 --> 00:02:21.220
<b>Episode 11</b>

00:02:15.420 --> 00:02:21.220
"Don't Think, Just Run!"

00:02:28.770 --> 00:02:31.310
The choice is yours, Tiffa.

00:02:32.860 --> 00:02:36.690
To save your friend, what is it that you should do?

00:02:36.780 --> 00:02:40.660
Making the right decision here is also in your own best interests.

00:02:47.450 --> 00:02:48.830
Captain!

00:02:49.500 --> 00:02:50.120
Where's Tiffa?

00:02:50.160 --> 00:02:51.040
What?!

00:02:51.580 --> 00:02:52.420
Tiffa!

00:02:57.760 --> 00:03:00.220
You made the right decision, Tiffa.

00:03:05.430 --> 00:03:06.310
Tiffa!

00:03:07.600 --> 00:03:09.770
Please, tell Garrod for me...

00:03:10.230 --> 00:03:11.480
Tell him I said goodbye.

00:03:11.520 --> 00:03:13.190
Wait, Tiffa!

00:03:23.320 --> 00:03:26.530
A split second longer, and I could have seen the boy die.

00:03:27.790 --> 00:03:31.910
Still... I wonder what a Bertigo is doing in a place like this?

00:03:37.250 --> 00:03:38.750
Are you okay over there?

00:03:39.420 --> 00:03:41.550
I'm more worried about him.

00:03:54.440 --> 00:03:57.650
Ow! Could you try to be a little gentler?

00:03:58.440 --> 00:04:00.400
I'm being plenty gentle.

00:04:00.690 --> 00:04:04.030
Careful, dummy! You're twisting it!

00:04:04.160 --> 00:04:05.530
Wrap it right!

00:04:05.660 --> 00:04:07.780
If you don't like it, do it yourself.

00:04:12.250 --> 00:04:14.000
What is Garrod's condition?

00:04:14.120 --> 00:04:16.960
I'm not concerned about his injuries. However...

00:04:23.720 --> 00:04:28.600
Psychologically, he's in bad shape. He must've had a terrifying experience.

00:04:33.020 --> 00:04:35.650
My prediction came true.

00:04:35.730 --> 00:04:41.030
Yes. I can't believe that the Newtype we were looking for attacked us.

00:04:41.440 --> 00:04:45.360
And to top it off, if his sweetie also got abducted...

00:04:45.610 --> 00:04:49.620
You're right! Let's get Tiffa back before he wakes up!

00:04:49.950 --> 00:04:52.200
It won't sit right with me if we don't!

00:04:52.290 --> 00:04:54.870
Your Gundams are still being repaired.

00:04:58.580 --> 00:05:00.920
Okay, let's pick up the pace, folks.

00:05:01.550 --> 00:05:05.130
If I see anyone slacking off, I'll throw something at him.

00:05:16.020 --> 00:05:17.350
Hey, right!

00:05:18.230 --> 00:05:20.360
New gear for the GX?

00:05:20.480 --> 00:05:25.700
Yeah. I've been considering it for a while, but I think now's the time.

00:05:26.360 --> 00:05:29.120
It's true that the Satellite Cannon is an incredible weapon,

00:05:29.160 --> 00:05:32.830
but it's just too powerful, and it can only be used at certain times, right?

00:05:33.370 --> 00:05:38.870
I think we need variations that will allow for more flexible responses.

00:05:40.960 --> 00:05:42.590
Okay, I'll authorize it.

00:05:42.670 --> 00:05:44.420
Awesome!

00:05:44.510 --> 00:05:47.050
I'm gonna get started right away!

00:05:47.170 --> 00:05:48.630
Just a moment.

00:05:51.300 --> 00:05:54.100
So, what did you want to discuss that's so important?

00:05:56.060 --> 00:05:57.140
What are you here for, Kid?

00:05:57.440 --> 00:05:58.350
Well...

00:05:58.890 --> 00:06:01.900
The thing is, I have a favor to ask of you two.

00:06:08.070 --> 00:06:12.030
It's Cdr. Carris! Cdr. Carris has returned!

00:06:12.660 --> 00:06:15.120
I hear Cdr. Carris drove off another bunch of Vultures!

00:06:15.620 --> 00:06:17.000
And that's not all!

00:06:17.620 --> 00:06:20.960
He also rescued that girl there who was being held prisoner by the Vultures!

00:06:21.210 --> 00:06:23.420
Cdr. Carris! Cdr. Carris!

00:06:23.590 --> 00:06:25.920
As long as Cdr. Carris is here, Fort Severn is safe!

00:06:26.010 --> 00:06:28.090
Yeah, because he's a Newtype!

00:06:28.920 --> 00:06:31.840
It won't do for you to look so frightened.

00:06:32.140 --> 00:06:35.810
As far as they are concerned, I just saved your life.

00:06:37.270 --> 00:06:40.560
Carris, it looks like you successfully completed your mission.

00:06:40.600 --> 00:06:44.520
Yes. However, I'm being held up by the citizens.

00:06:44.610 --> 00:06:47.690
It might take a while to get back.

00:06:48.940 --> 00:06:52.740
Our good citizens all adore you.

00:06:59.410 --> 00:07:01.620
Please be patient for a little longer.

00:07:02.120 --> 00:07:05.250
What do you plan to do with me?

00:07:05.590 --> 00:07:08.380
We're going to make you a savior along with me.

00:07:15.300 --> 00:07:17.930
That idiot is moping too much.

00:07:18.930 --> 00:07:21.270
That's true, but still...

00:07:21.690 --> 00:07:25.900
When you get trounced that thoroughly, it's only natural to fall into a funk.

00:07:26.020 --> 00:07:29.190
Newtypes sure are powerful...

00:07:29.940 --> 00:07:32.910
It would've been nice if Jamil had given us a heads-up.

00:07:32.990 --> 00:07:35.410
He used to be a Newtype, right?

00:07:35.490 --> 00:07:37.080
Yeah, but he...

00:07:37.660 --> 00:07:41.870
We all have many questions regarding Newtypes that we want to ask him.

00:07:41.960 --> 00:07:45.920
But I can't bring myself to ask him, not when the Captain's powers...

00:07:45.920 --> 00:07:50.550
...resulted in the deaths of so many and cause him such suffering.

00:07:55.550 --> 00:07:57.390
Are you okay, Jamil?

00:07:58.850 --> 00:08:01.180
This... isn't going to be easy.

00:08:01.680 --> 00:08:04.020
Maybe you shouldn't push yourself so hard.

00:08:04.100 --> 00:08:06.190
That isn't an option.

00:08:06.310 --> 00:08:09.150
Not when I think about Tiffa being held prisoner.

00:08:13.030 --> 00:08:15.320
These will be your quarters from now on.

00:08:16.280 --> 00:08:18.620
Do you like them? Not bad, eh?

00:08:22.620 --> 00:08:24.170
You don't care for them?

00:08:26.250 --> 00:08:27.840
I will return later, then.

00:08:38.970 --> 00:08:43.350
What do you mean? Why am I not allowed to interact with her?

00:08:43.480 --> 00:08:46.400
Because the two of you have identical powers.

00:08:48.310 --> 00:08:50.690
Until I have more concrete data,

00:08:50.820 --> 00:08:54.780
I have no idea how your powers might resonate.

00:08:55.360 --> 00:08:57.030
I see.

00:08:57.820 --> 00:08:59.120
You disagree?

00:08:59.240 --> 00:09:01.450
No, sir. Of course not.

00:09:01.580 --> 00:09:05.960
This is to unify the world. Set your feelings aside and focus on the goal.

00:09:06.920 --> 00:09:08.250
Yes, sir.

00:09:08.750 --> 00:09:11.210
More importantly, don't let your guard down.

00:09:11.300 --> 00:09:15.170
It's possible that those Vultures will attempt to rescue her.

00:09:18.470 --> 00:09:20.600
Nobody sleeps until we're done!

00:09:20.720 --> 00:09:23.720
When you're exhausted, collapse where you're standing!

00:09:25.270 --> 00:09:27.230
I don't mean to make you feel indebted,

00:09:27.350 --> 00:09:30.230
but we're working ourselves to death for you, Gundam Boy.

00:09:37.570 --> 00:09:38.530
Captain?

00:09:39.110 --> 00:09:40.120
Status report.

00:09:40.620 --> 00:09:44.080
Three more days are required to complete upgrades to the GX.

00:09:45.250 --> 00:09:48.870
When we factor in the time needed for Garrod to train with the new systems,

00:09:48.960 --> 00:09:51.090
we must be prepared to wait a while.

00:09:51.380 --> 00:09:52.500
I see.

00:09:52.590 --> 00:09:56.420
Also, Garrod is still spacing out.

00:09:56.920 --> 00:09:59.930
I guess we won't be rescuing Tiffa anytime soon.

00:10:00.390 --> 00:10:02.220
I'm worried.

00:10:02.300 --> 00:10:04.520
It's not just Tiffa that I'm worried about.

00:10:05.520 --> 00:10:07.850
There are also these two Gundams that have been hunting us.

00:10:08.850 --> 00:10:11.650
We only managed to escape their attacks this far...

00:10:11.730 --> 00:10:15.990
...because we had the GX, the Airmaster, and the Leopard.

00:10:16.530 --> 00:10:20.240
I hear that repairs on the Airmaster and Leopard are almost finished,

00:10:20.530 --> 00:10:22.530
but those two won't be enough on their own.

00:10:22.700 --> 00:10:25.490
Things don't look good for us, do they?

00:10:44.560 --> 00:10:47.520
It's been too long, Deputy Director-General Aimzat.

00:10:48.020 --> 00:10:50.350
I'm happy to see that you two are looking well.

00:10:51.400 --> 00:10:55.150
We're most indebted to you, for personally overseeing our resupply.

00:10:55.360 --> 00:10:56.980
So, how are things progressing on your end?

00:10:57.570 --> 00:11:00.820
The Committee has finally gotten their lazy asses into gear.

00:11:00.910 --> 00:11:04.620
It won't be long now before the New U.N.E. Government is formed.

00:11:04.910 --> 00:11:06.450
At last...

00:11:06.580 --> 00:11:11.330
We intend to stop at nothing until the day our objectives are met.

00:11:12.630 --> 00:11:15.590
They don't suspect your true identities, I trust?

00:11:15.670 --> 00:11:20.550
You needn't worry. We're simple freelance mobile suit pilots to them.

00:11:20.630 --> 00:11:24.050
As well as their archenemies.

00:11:24.890 --> 00:11:28.520
The Committee has grave concerns regarding the Freeden's activities.

00:11:28.560 --> 00:11:32.520
Newtypes will be indispensable to the New U.N.E.

00:11:32.850 --> 00:11:34.860
We're letting them run free.

00:11:34.980 --> 00:11:38.730
They're using Tiffa Adill to gather Newtypes.

00:11:39.320 --> 00:11:41.700
And when the time is right...

00:11:41.820 --> 00:11:45.570
You will launch an all-out attack and take them all, eh?

00:11:45.660 --> 00:11:48.660
Including Tiffa Adill, of course.

00:11:49.160 --> 00:11:51.710
Yes, but there is one point of concern.

00:11:52.160 --> 00:11:56.920
After Tiffa Adill fell into their hands, they began amassing mobile suits.

00:11:57.040 --> 00:12:00.210
Perhaps we should act before they become too powerful.

00:12:00.550 --> 00:12:02.590
I'll leave that decision to you.

00:12:02.630 --> 00:12:03.930
Understood.

00:12:04.760 --> 00:12:06.550
Good luck on your mission, then.

00:12:06.550 --> 00:12:07.350
Yes, sir. Yes, sir.

00:12:12.230 --> 00:12:14.190
Are we going to do it, Brother?

00:12:14.310 --> 00:12:17.480
Of course. We're going to destroy their Gundams.

00:12:51.930 --> 00:12:53.430
It's because we're the same.

00:12:54.390 --> 00:12:56.850
It's because we have the same powers that I'm-

00:13:13.660 --> 00:13:15.580
It looks like you're ahead of schedule.

00:13:15.660 --> 00:13:18.040
Yeah, because we've been working around the clock.

00:13:21.500 --> 00:13:25.010
Hey, Doc! I've got another man down over here!

00:13:25.720 --> 00:13:27.470
I'll see to him after this one!

00:13:28.550 --> 00:13:29.970
I hate to make you do this.

00:13:30.050 --> 00:13:33.220
Don't sweat it, they're doing this because they want to.

00:13:33.310 --> 00:13:37.480
But Gundam Boy still hasn't bounced back, right?

00:13:37.770 --> 00:13:38.350
No.

00:13:39.100 --> 00:13:40.190
He's all yours.

00:13:40.310 --> 00:13:44.280
Even if we finish here, it'll be for nothing if we don't have a pilot.

00:13:44.860 --> 00:13:46.200
I know.

00:14:02.460 --> 00:14:04.090
We need to talk.

00:14:17.180 --> 00:14:19.230
It's done...

00:14:21.360 --> 00:14:25.980
Oops! You're the last of the mechanic squad to drop.

00:14:29.150 --> 00:14:32.320
You're an impressive little kid.

00:14:33.950 --> 00:14:34.830
What is it?!

00:14:34.950 --> 00:14:38.500
Mobile suits spotted dead ahead! All hands to battle stations!

00:14:41.880 --> 00:14:44.840
Olba. How many times have you fought in snow?

00:14:45.090 --> 00:14:49.090
Four times. But all in a simulator.

00:14:49.220 --> 00:14:51.590
Then you have more experience than I do.

00:14:54.100 --> 00:14:55.810
Guys, this is bad!

00:14:55.890 --> 00:14:58.520
There's no sign of the Captain or Garrod anywhere!

00:14:59.100 --> 00:15:00.560
They've both vanished?

00:15:01.230 --> 00:15:04.310
Maybe they eloped together? Nah, I doubt that...

00:15:04.400 --> 00:15:05.480
Get serious!

00:15:05.940 --> 00:15:06.900
Sorry!

00:15:07.480 --> 00:15:10.320
Captain, where have you gone?

00:15:13.820 --> 00:15:15.030
You're pathetic.

00:15:15.780 --> 00:15:18.120
Look at you, moping just because your girl was stolen from you!

00:15:18.120 --> 00:15:19.290
That's not why!

00:15:19.710 --> 00:15:20.710
Then what is it?

00:15:21.750 --> 00:15:25.920
I didn't expect that a Newtype would be that powerful.

00:15:27.250 --> 00:15:31.380
Plus, I don't have any special powers...

00:15:32.760 --> 00:15:35.050
Special powers, huh?

00:15:41.350 --> 00:15:43.730
Don't forget your you-know-whats!

00:15:43.850 --> 00:15:47.400
How could I forget something that they tailor-made for me?

00:15:56.330 --> 00:15:57.740
Don't wipe out!

00:15:57.780 --> 00:16:01.460
And don't you face plant like before.

00:16:02.000 --> 00:16:02.830
Here they come!

00:16:05.750 --> 00:16:07.840
The GX isn't launching?

00:16:07.880 --> 00:16:11.920
Brother, they've made cold-weather modifications.

00:16:13.180 --> 00:16:17.390
Those two again! I can't believe they followed us all the way up here!

00:16:20.770 --> 00:16:23.520
It isn't a good idea to underestimate us.

00:16:27.190 --> 00:16:29.780
I'll make some red flowers bloom on the snow fields.

00:16:30.570 --> 00:16:33.530
Don't be so clingy, you creepy Gundams!

00:16:39.830 --> 00:16:41.790
What's that sound?!

00:16:41.870 --> 00:16:43.290
You're hearing things.

00:16:45.210 --> 00:16:46.580
Hey, don't push yourself!

00:16:46.750 --> 00:16:49.420
I'm a professional mechanic.

00:16:49.920 --> 00:16:52.550
I just have to make cockpit adjustments.

00:16:53.420 --> 00:16:56.180
I swear, no one ever listens to me.

00:17:01.560 --> 00:17:05.020
What is this? A frozen lake?

00:17:05.600 --> 00:17:09.480
Would you mind returning the GX's control unit to me?

00:17:10.270 --> 00:17:12.940
You don't need it anymore, right?

00:17:24.250 --> 00:17:25.870
What are you doing?!

00:17:28.500 --> 00:17:30.170
I'll give you one last chance.

00:17:31.000 --> 00:17:31.960
Last chance?

00:17:32.250 --> 00:17:35.170
If you want to come back to the ship, go fetch that.

00:17:35.920 --> 00:17:39.720
Don't be stupid! If the ice breaks, I'll die!

00:17:40.300 --> 00:17:42.140
But you don't need special powers.

00:18:16.170 --> 00:18:17.130
What?!

00:18:27.520 --> 00:18:28.480
Oh, crap!

00:18:32.020 --> 00:18:32.690
Look out!

00:18:32.730 --> 00:18:33.770
This will be close!

00:18:37.610 --> 00:18:38.400
What was that?!

00:18:38.450 --> 00:18:39.450
Oh, crap!

00:19:28.660 --> 00:19:30.870
I'm through being your punching bag!

00:19:33.250 --> 00:19:34.540
I won't lose to you!

00:19:45.390 --> 00:19:49.180
How long do you think you can go without sleep?! You have to rest!

00:19:53.100 --> 00:19:55.770
That woke me up a bit...

00:19:55.860 --> 00:19:57.150
Kid...

00:20:08.120 --> 00:20:09.950
Damn it! I'm out of ammo?

00:20:12.460 --> 00:20:13.170
Roabea!

00:20:17.420 --> 00:20:19.670
Out of bullets and out of steam, huh?

00:20:23.220 --> 00:20:25.720
You've grown too powerful.

00:20:26.050 --> 00:20:27.850
So you have to die.

00:20:32.810 --> 00:20:34.140
I got it!

00:20:34.730 --> 00:20:37.150
I got it, I got it, I got it!

00:20:39.570 --> 00:20:41.110
Garrod!

00:20:41.320 --> 00:20:42.780
Run!

00:20:42.900 --> 00:20:44.110
Jamil?!

00:20:44.650 --> 00:20:46.780
Don't think, just run!

00:21:08.850 --> 00:21:11.010
I thought I was a goner...

00:21:12.810 --> 00:21:16.230
I'll run! I'll run without thinking!

00:21:18.150 --> 00:21:19.360
Let's head back.

00:21:20.020 --> 00:21:21.360
Everyone is waiting.

00:21:27.110 --> 00:21:28.160
They're back!

00:21:32.330 --> 00:21:33.620
Just in time...

00:21:38.460 --> 00:21:39.170
Kid!

00:21:39.830 --> 00:21:41.380
Let me worry about him.

00:22:00.110 --> 00:22:01.110
Crap...

00:22:01.150 --> 00:22:04.190
We're out of everything else, so now we're out of time?

00:22:05.070 --> 00:22:05.570
Brother!

00:22:05.610 --> 00:22:06.400
What?!

00:22:09.320 --> 00:22:10.490
That little twerp!

00:22:10.740 --> 00:22:12.490
He's stealing our thunder!

00:22:17.500 --> 00:22:19.250
Is he all right now?

00:22:19.830 --> 00:22:21.710
Don't worry about Garrod.

00:22:30.430 --> 00:22:32.720
Brother, the GX, it's-

00:22:32.760 --> 00:22:35.350
I don't believe it... It's been upgraded?

00:22:35.470 --> 00:22:37.680
Let's do this!

00:22:45.610 --> 00:22:50.910
<b>Can I find the words to tell you</b>

00:22:48.350 --> 00:22:53.910
To rescue Tiffa, Garrod infiltrates Fort Severn by himself.

00:22:50.910 --> 00:22:56.290
<b>How I live between the walls of steel and stone</b>

00:22:53.910 --> 00:23:03.630
What awaits him there is twisted hatred caused by the war and a shocking truth about Carris.

00:22:57.950 --> 00:23:04.130
<b>How I close my eyes to find some kind of rapture</b>

00:23:04.840 --> 00:23:10.470
<b>In a world where you can feel so all alone</b>

00:23:12.140 --> 00:23:17.470
<b>Inside I'm full of light and laughter</b>

00:23:18.930 --> 00:23:21.350
<b>There's a flame that burns in me</b>

00:23:21.350 --> 00:23:22.310
<b>(I need a way)</b>

00:23:22.310 --> 00:23:26.400
<b>(I need a way) I need a way to set it free</b>

00:23:26.400 --> 00:23:31.320
<b>When you find love in your heart</b>

00:23:31.320 --> 00:23:33.450
<b>(The human touch)</b>

00:23:33.450 --> 00:23:37.490
<b>You can believe from the start</b>

00:23:37.490 --> 00:23:39.500
<b>(From the start)</b>

